              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for the weekly, then the French for the subscriber."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: rédiger",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rédiger — \"to write, to draft (a text)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le journaliste a rédigé son article en une heure. The journalist wrote his article in an hour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For a text with a purpose: rédiger une lettre, un rapport. In daily speech, écrire."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rédiger is a learned borrowing from Latin redigere \"to bring back, to reduce to order\" (EtymDB), from red- \"back\" and agere \"to drive\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
